SUMMARY:Scenic AVL  - Waynesville Way - Weekend Wildcard
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nRating: Strenuous for Distance\nDi
 stance: 9 mile\nElevation Gain: 1000 feet\, in small chunk\nFeatures: Rura
 l farm views\, neighborhood charm\, nice downtown\nWildlife: No bears\, bu
 t there are lots of birds and a few cows\nPace: 3.2 mph\nSurface : Road\n\
 nCarpooling: Please announce in the chat if you would like to carpool. I r
 ecommend 8:25 from 16 Regent Park Blvd\, Asheville (near Sam's Club)\, but
  I am coming from Hendersonville\, so I won't be there.\n\nNO BATHROOM at 
 the start.\n\nDogs: On leash\nRoute:[ Waynesville Wa](https://www.alltrail
 s.com/explore/recording/activity-november-11-2024-5e38810)\n[ ](https://ma
 ps.app.goo.gl/drFxX2TaTrZKWX9F8)\nCoffee Break: 10:15 at Panacea coffee ho
 use. If you want to sleep in\, meet at Panacea. There's a free parking lot
  on Montgomery Street nearby.[ https://maps.app.goo.gl/7Cw7n9YHtPvmLLaD](h
 ttps://maps.app.goo.gl/7Cw7n9YHtPvmLLaD8)\n\nMountain Research Station: We
  are walking down Test Farm Road across the NC Agricultural Extension Moun
 tain Research Station. Please sign in using the[ Visitor Registratio](http
 s://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfDFCDqvA7x7AkL8A2jaLthTf2lSQBwlEyC99
 r-H4SVDsqQaA/viewform)n website\n\nScenic Asheville Series: This hike is a
  wildcard \, meaning that it can be a substitute for any of the other hike
 s\nThere are[ 10 hikes](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_Ohx
 KIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?usp=drivesdk) in the series\; hike 
 9 of them and receive an[ attractive badge](https://docs.google.com/drawin
 gs/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for your pack. Bad
 gers can always attend a hike\, even if on the waiting list. See our[ high
 lights her](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/18cFp2Uhw8XthOFXxekBpt2
 LGP6ww-V7kmXQExI7Y0h0/)e\n\nCall (do not text) the hike leader on the day 
 of the hike if you can't find the start 828-290-088\n\nDisclaimer and Rele
 ase of Liability\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may h
 ave traffic. Participants are responsible for their safety on streets and 
 trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional g
 uide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you 
 sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and v
 oluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages
  arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In additi
 on\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms:[ https://www.meet
 up.com/term](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
