SUMMARY:Scenic AVL #7: Scott Mountain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThere is very limited parking at t
 he [trailhead](https://maps.app.goo.gl/fETct2fiMiLz1HEG8). Please plan to 
 meet at Lake Hills Church parking lot at 10 minutes before the start to co
 ndense cars.\nWe will meet in the parking lot area close to the intersecti
 on of Lake Drive and Black Midge lane.\n\nLake Hills Church Parking Lot is
  pictured above.\n- [https://maps.app.goo.gl/X1TctrhYv3gihmh66](https://ma
 ps.app.goo.gl/X1TctrhYv3gihmh66)\n*Call the hike leader at 828-290-0886 if
  you cannot find us. Do not text.\n\n**Rating**: Moderate\n**Elevation**: 
 800\n**Distance**: 5 miles\n**Surface**: Trail\n**Pace**: 3 mph\n**Dogs**:
  on leash.\n**Gear**: Long pants recommended\, bug spray\, water. The tick
 s are bad on this trail. Bring your bug spray !\n**Features**: wooded trai
 l\, interesting plants and fungi. Bears are shy\, but we may see them\, al
 so deer and squirrels. 3 miles uphill\, 2.25 down.\n**All Trails Route**:\
 n[Scott Mountain Loop on AllTrails](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/
 scott-mountain-loop-4217403?p=-1&sh=ifwm3x)\n\n[Scenic Asheville Series](h
 ttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_
 NEjjI5Lk): there are 9 hikes in the series\, plus a few wild cards. Hike 9
  of them and receive an [attractive](https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1g
 oXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) badge for your backpack. 
 If you have a badge \, you can always come on\na hike \, even if you are o
 n the waiting list .\n\n**Guests**: Make sure your guests are fit enough t
 o complete the hike. if someone is a guest\, their hike will not count tow
 ard a badge because there will not be a record of their name .\n\nDisclaim
 er and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiking on city street
 s that may have traffic. Participants are responsible for their safety on 
 streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a pr
 ofessional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this t
 rip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you 
 freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\,
  and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this even
 t. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [http
 s://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
